book tuple_arrays
read everything from nil.std.collections

counter begin record
    field total as number
end record

repeat-pair of type T receives item as T returns array of T begin paragraph
    value values as array of T is new-with-value of T with size being 2, `value` being item
    append item to values
    give values
end paragraph

make-owned returns array of tuple of (number, text) begin paragraph
    value values as array of tuple of (number, text) is []
    variable index as override integer is 0
    repeat while index is less than 257
        value entry as tuple of (number, text) is (index, formatted "owned-{index}")
        append entry to values
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat
    give values
end paragraph

fresh-pairs returns array of tuple of (number, text) begin paragraph
    give [(1, "returned"), ((2 becomes number), "wide")]
end paragraph

main returns override integer begin paragraph
    value first as tuple of (number, text, floating, boolean) is (41, "first", -1.5, true)
    value second as tuple of (number, text, floating, boolean) is (42, "second", 2.25, false)
    value items is [first, second]
    value alias is items
    value retained is items at 0
    say the length of items
    say (items at 0).0
    say (items at 1).1
    say (items at 0).2
    say (items at 1).3
    set items at 0 to second
    say (alias at 0).0
    say retained.1
    append first to alias
    say the length of items
    say (items at 2).1
    set items at -1 to first
    set items at 3 to second
    say the length of items
    say (items at 0).0

    value nested is [((1, "nested"), (false, -0.5)), ((2, "tail"), (true, 0.25))]
    say (nested at 0).0.1
    say (nested at 1).1.0
    say (nested at 0).1.1
    value singles as array of tuple of (number) is [((9 becomes number),), ((10 becomes number),)]
    say (singles at 1).0

    value object is build counter with total being 5
    value references is [(object, "shared")]
    value saved is references at 0
    set saved.0.total to 17
    say (references at 0).0.total
    set references at 0 to ((build counter with total being 23), "replacement")
    say saved.0.total
    say (references at 0).0.total

    value repeated is repeat-pair of tuple of (number, text, floating, boolean) with item being first
    say length of tuple of (number, text, floating, boolean) with arr being repeated
    evaluate array-set of tuple of (number, text, floating, boolean) with arr being repeated, idx being 1, `value` being second
    value selected is get of tuple of (number, text, floating, boolean) with arr being repeated, idx being 1
    say selected.1
    evaluate array-set of tuple of (number, text, floating, boolean) with arr being repeated, idx being -1, `value` being second
    evaluate array-set of tuple of (number, text, floating, boolean) with arr being repeated, idx being 3, `value` being second
    say (repeated at 0).1
    say try-copy-range of tuple of (number, text, floating, boolean) with source being repeated, source-offset being 0, destination being repeated, destination-offset being 1, count being 2
    say (repeated at 1).1
    say (repeated at 2).1
    say try-copy-range of tuple of (number, text, floating, boolean) with source being repeated, source-offset being 1, destination being repeated, destination-offset being 0, count being 2
    say (repeated at 0).1
    say (repeated at 1).1
    say try-copy-range of tuple of (number, text, floating, boolean) with source being repeated, source-offset being 0, destination being repeated, destination-offset being 2, count being 2
    say (repeated at 2).1

    value empty as array of tuple of (number, text, floating, boolean) is []
    say the length of empty
    append second to empty
    say (empty at 0).0
    value filled is new-with-value of tuple of (counter, text) with size being 2, `value` being (object, "filled")
    set (filled at 0).0.total to 31
    say (filled at 1).0.total
    say object.total
    value returned-values is make-owned with nothing
    value owned-alias is returned-values
    value first-owned is returned-values at 0
    append ((257 becomes number), "added") to owned-alias
    say the length of returned-values
    say first-owned.1
    say (returned-values at 128).1
    say (returned-values at 256).0
    say (returned-values at 257).1
    value converted as array of tuple of (number, text) is [(1, "declared"), ((2 becomes number), "wide")]
    set converted at 0 to (3, "replaced")
    append (4, "pushed") to converted
    say (converted at 0).0
    say (converted at 2).0
    value returned-pairs is fresh-pairs with nothing
    say (returned-pairs at 0).1
    say (returned-pairs at 1).0
    give 0
end paragraph
